{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8e1a4c498e3f76010419866815b8638d0f6becba1009f62497513a8148004958","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciler inbound-apply path","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","_inbound_update_write_status_event","_inbound_create_write_status_event","_cascade_inbound_status_parents","_CASCADING_EDGES","_resolve_parent_in_status","rebar._commands.transition","docs/concurrency.md","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py","STATUS","_write_event_file"],"problem_keywords":["parent-first cascade","inbound reconcile","status write","invalid state","closed parent","active child","invariant violation"],"propositions":["Inbound Jira status writes bypass the parent-first cascade mechanism, allowing a closed parent to hold an active child—an I4a-invalid state.","The inbound-apply path must share the same cascading-edge decision table and parent-eligibility logic as the interactive cascade, single-sourced from rebar._commands.transition.","When an inbound status change moves a child into an active state, eligible ancestors' STATUS events must be written first (topmost first, cycle-guarded) via the same _write_event_file primitive.","Same-status inbound status writes must be suppressed as no-ops to maintain batch self-consistency and idempotency when a cascaded parent is later mutated.","Inbound status writes must NOT route through transition_compute to preserve determinism and avoid imposing the LLM start-work gate on reconcile batches."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":178